if you're anything like me then you've  spent a lot of time using youtube to  listen to video game music for years  listening to game music on services like  spotify was basically impossible and  while things have gotten better youtube  is still the best place to go if you  want to listen to your favorite game  soundtrack or it was until last week  when the biggest most important uploader  of video game music on the entire  internet got barry in over 3 000  copyright claims and deleted his channel  alright so before we give the video i  just want to remind you all to please  sub to the channel and turn on  notifications if you haven't done it yet  because it really does help okay so if  you've ever used youtube to listen to  video game music you probably recognize  this guy his channel was called gill the  center and for over a decade it was the  go-to place to listen to video game  music on youtube but now if you try to  go to his channel all you get is a  stupid monkey that's because last week  he shut down his channel after he  received 3  500 copyright blocks from nintendo in  two days now you might be thinking to  yourself how on earth do you get 3 500  copyright blocks in two days  well when you upload game music you  don't own to youtube it kind of makes  sense you've got albums with what 20 30  songs on them sometimes even more and  each song from those albums is its own  unique individual youtube video which  means each video gets its own copyright  block and it's not like this is the  first time this happened to gilda center  over the past few years he's posted  images of his email inbox whenever he  received copyright blocks from nintendo  just last month he got over 1 300 on  january 29th alone hell in 2013 nintendo  claimed 70 of his videos in one day now  obviously gilva center never owned any  of the music he was uploading and  nintendo was well within their rights to  take his videos down but i think the  reason so many people including myself  are really upset about his channel  disappearing is because it's a little  more complicated than that see i'm a  really big fan of video game soundtracks  yes i know i'm a nerd but i really do  think that there's a lot of great music  in video games that's honestly sometimes  really hard to listen to like back in  the day if i wanted to listen to route  209 the best song in pokemon history  legally the only way i could do that  would be to turn on my ds turn on  pokemon pearl and bike out to the part  of the map where that song plays that's  because for years most video games just  didn't release cd soundtracks in the  west some games got exclusive  soundtracks in japan but those were  really expensive to import  so anybody who liked video game music  had to turn to piracy back then we  downloaded mp3s from the internet used  itunes to stick them on our ipods in  middle school and i know i'm dating  myself here but the point is that i  don't have a dedicated mp3 player  anymore  no one does we all stream our music  these days so that form of piracy is  basically obsolete and for the most part  video game publishers have only very  recently started putting their  soundtracks onto services like spotify  it's amazing that so much stuff is there  but a lot of songs aren't specifically  songs owned by nintendo which is why for  basically as long as youtube has existed  there have been channels dedicated to  uploading video game music for those of  us who want to listen to our favorite  songs but don't have dedicated mp3  players anymore and don't want to pay 65  to import a cd box sec also what would i  even listen to a cd on these days i  haven't had a cd drive in my computer  since 2014. anyway my point is that  there are hundreds if not thousands of  channels on youtube dedicated to ripping  and uploading video game music  specifically nintendo music and  gilbasunner was by far the biggest  before he took his channel down gilba  center had 6400 uploads 1.5 billion  views and was doing around 19 million  views a month basically gilda center was  kind of huge  and now the original gilva center  channel is gone literally wiped off the  face of youtube i know that ultimately  there are a ton of other channels you  can go to to listen to video game music  including some of the very tracks that  got copyright blocked on gilvasunner's  channel but i think what the channel's  deletion represents is really important  like i said earlier there was this era  of youtube where it was just the wild  west everyone is uploading movies and tv  shows and music they didn't own and it  lived alongside home movies and reaction  videos like the weirdest internet  library over the years youtube decided  they wanted to make money so they  started to run ads and clamped down hard  on piracy and while i get it i think  what it's led to is kind of sad there is  no good convenient legal way to listen  to music from nintendo games right now  for years that was also true about music  from companies like square enix capcom  and sega but these days if you search  spotify you'll find plenty of the  greatest video game albums of all time  meanwhile if you search for nintendo  music all you get are crappy covers  youtube is the place to go if you want  to listen to nintendo's contributions to  this art form i know it sounds like i'm  standing here defending piracy but i  literally am the fact of the matter is  the community saw that nintendo wasn't  doing a good job of preserving their own  history so they took matters into their  own hands gilbert center said it best  himself back in 2019 if companies like  nintendo felt so entitled to block his  videos why not work on actually getting  those songs up somewhere people can  legally listen to them it should have  been clear to them that fans would be  interested based on how many views gilba  center was getting oh and while we're  talking about nintendo let's do a quick  aside there was a thread going around  last week of people speculating that the  nintendo that blocked gilda center's  videos might not have actually been  nintendo but instead was a troll  pretending to be them youtube has since  stepped in to confirm that it was  actually nintendo that put out the  thousands of claims on gilbert center's  channel and i wanted to bring this up  because one it's important to clear the  air so everyone knows what's actually  going on here but also because two this  is absurd this is one of the biggest  gaming companies in the world going  after one random dutch dude's youtube  channel obviously they feel like they  have to do this for legal reasons but  come on gilvasunner is not the first  person to upload game music he didn't  own to youtube and he is definitely not  going to be the last at least not while  companies like nintendo are being weird  holdouts about getting their music onto  platforms people actually use what are  they gonna do keep sending thousands of  copyright strikes to random youtube  channels anytime a new one pops up this  channel wasn't gilva center's livelihood  i can't imagine he made any money off of  it at all but i bet the reason he kept  it running for over a decade was because  he and anybody who ever ended up on his  channel after searching for a random  song  loved listening to video game music so  this is just gonna keep happening either  until they finally kill the old youtube  and break people's love for video game  music or until companies like nintendo  wake up realize it's 2022 and start  uploading things themselves  [Music]  ludwig does 31 million so that's not it  holy [ __ ]  yeah the my i stand on the stool and it  just gave out under me  oh my god that was terrifying  yeah i am fine i think this stool has  maybe served  its purpose in life  [Music]
 

